<main>
<section class="hero"><div class="wrap">
 <h1>Four pillars. One unified profile.</h1>
 <p class="lead">Most health tools do one of these. VitaCrypt does all four, and the value is in how they compound.</p>
 <ul class="grid g4 pils" aria-label="The four pillars">
  <li><a class="tile pil" href="#unified"><span class="sq"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3l9 5-9 5-9-5 9-5zM3 13l9 5 9-5"/></svg></span><h3>Unified</h3><p class="small">Every signal in one profile</p></a></li>
  <li><a class="tile pil" href="#evidence"><span class="sq"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 4h11a3 3 0 0 1 3 3v13H8a3 3 0 0 1-3-3V4zM8 17h11"/></svg></span><h3>Cited</h3><p class="small">Every claim, a real source</p></a></li>
  <li><a class="tile pil" href="#personalized"><span class="sq"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="8" r="4"/><path d="M4 21c0-4 4-6 8-6s8 2 8 6"/></svg></span><h3>Personalized</h3><p class="small">Your genes, your air</p></a></li>
  <li><a class="tile pil" href="#encrypted"><span class="sq"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="5" y="11" width="14" height="10" rx="2"/><path d="M8 11V8a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v3"/></svg></span><h3>Private</h3><p class="small">Encrypted, and honest about it</p></a></li>
 </ul>
 <div class="cta"><a class="btn p" href="/beta">Apply for the beta</a><a class="tb" href="/agent">See the Lab Agent</a></div>
<details><summary>More on the four pillars</summary><div><p>A unified data fabric built to ingest any health signal; every recommendation cited to live science; personalization down to your genotype and local environment; and privacy built in by design, so what leaves the app is kept small and logged.</p></div></details>
</div></section>

<section id="failures"><div class="wrap">
 <h2>The four failures we replace</h2>
 <ul class="grid g4 fails">
  <li class="tile"><span class="sq"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 4h6v6H4zM14 4h6v6h-6zM4 14h6v6H4zM14 14h6v6h-6z"/></svg></span><h3>Fragmentation</h3><p class="small">Each tool holds a piece. The patterns live between them.</p></li>
  <li class="tile"><span class="sq"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 12s4-7 10-7 10 7 10 7-4 7-10 7S2 12 2 12z"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/></svg></span><h3>Exposed in the clear</h3><p class="small">Full records go to every vendor. The Lab Agent sends only what a step needs and logs it.</p></li>
  <li class="tile"><span class="sq"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="9" cy="8" r="3"/><circle cx="17" cy="9" r="2.500"/><path d="M3 20c0-3 3-5 6-5s6 2 6 5M16 15c3 0 5 1.500 5 4"/></svg></span><h3>Generic advice</h3><p class="small">Written for the median person, not your genotype.</p></li>
  <li class="tile"><span class="sq"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 18a4 4 0 1 1 .8-7.900A5 5 0 0 1 17 9a4.500 4.500 0 0 1 0 9H7z"/></svg></span><h3>Environmental blindness</h3><p class="small">No tool fuses outdoor air with your biology.</p></li>
 </ul>
 <p class="cap">Older insight cards still send more than the Lab Agent does; <a href="/data">Your data</a> lists it.</p>
</div></section>

<section id="how"><div class="wrap">
 <h2>How it works: collect, unify, check, act</h2>
 <ol class="rail">
  <li><div class="st"><div><h3>Collect</h3><p>Upload labs, DNA and a gut report. Air and UV come from your city.</p></div><img src="/img/agent/demo-home.jpg" width="375" height="812" loading="lazy" alt="Lab Agent screen in the demo: a new lab report ready to check, with earlier labs listed"></div></li>
  <li><div class="st"><div><h3>Unify</h3><p>One profile, so a lab, a gene and a habit can be linked.</p></div><img src="/img/app/today-link-phone.jpg" width="780" height="885" loading="lazy" alt="Demo Today screen: vitamin D below range linked to Labs, DNA and Wearable, labelled Hypothesis"></div></li>
  <li><div class="st"><div><h3>Check</h3><p>Compare with your last lab and your DNA, then search the research.</p></div><img src="/img/agent/run-steps.jpg" width="525" height="1136" loading="lazy" alt="Lab Agent run in the demo: markers read, compared with the last lab, 13 searches and 52 papers found"></div></li>
  <li><div class="st"><div><h3>Act</h3><p>Habits, a dated retest and clinician questions, each with its source.</p></div><img src="/img/agent/plan.jpg" width="525" height="1136" loading="lazy" alt="Lab Agent plan in the demo: daily habits marked Cited or Hypothesis with PubMed links"></div></li>
 </ol>
 <p class="cap">Real screens from the demo. The person is fictional and the data is synthetic.</p>
 <p><a class="tb" href="/agent">Watch the live walkthrough</a></p>
</div></section>

<section id="unified"><div class="wrap">
 <h2>Every health signal, fused into one profile</h2>
 <p class="lead">Eight kinds of data, mapped into one schema. Encrypted at rest under a per-user key today.</p>
 <ul class="chips" aria-label="Sources in the profile">
  <li class="chip sm on-lab"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 3h6M10 3v11l-3.500 5a1.500 1.500 0 0 0 1.300 2.300h8.400a1.500 1.500 0 0 0 1.300-2.300L14 14V3"/></svg>Labs</li>
  <li class="chip sm on-dna"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 3c0 5 10 5 10 9s-10 4-10 9M17 3c0 5-10 5-10 9s10 4 10 9M9 7h6M9 17h6"/></svg>DNA</li>
  <li class="chip sm on-gut"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="9" cy="10" r="5"/><circle cx="17.500" cy="7.500" r="2.500"/><circle cx="16" cy="16.500" r="3.500"/></svg>Gut</li>
  <li class="chip sm on-body"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="4" y="4" width="16" height="16" rx="3"/><path d="M9 8.500h6M12 8.500v3"/></svg>Body</li>
  <li class="chip sm on-wear"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="6" y="7" width="12" height="10" rx="3"/><path d="M9 7l.500-4h5l.500 4M9 17l.500 4h5l.500-4"/></svg>Wearable</li>
  <li class="chip sm on-chk"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M8.500 14.500c1 1.200 2.200 1.800 3.500 1.800s2.500-.600 3.500-1.800M9 9.800v.400M15 9.800v.400"/></svg>Check-ins</li>
  <li class="chip sm on-sur"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="6" y="4" width="12" height="17" rx="2"/><path d="M9.500 9h5M9.500 13h5M9.500 17h3"/></svg>Surveys</li>
  <li class="chip sm on-air"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4"/><path d="M12 3v2M12 19v2M3 12h2M19 12h2M5.600 5.600l1.400 1.400M17 17l1.400 1.400M5.600 18.400L7 17M17 7l1.400-1.400"/></svg>Air &amp; UV</li>
 </ul>
 <h3 class="sub">How each gets in today <span class="tag">In the MVP</span></h3>
 <ul class="grid g2 rows">
  <li><span class="sq"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 3h6M10 3v11l-3.500 5a1.500 1.500 0 0 0 1.300 2.300h8.400a1.500 1.500 0 0 0 1.300-2.300L14 14V3"/></svg></span><div><h3>Labs</h3><p>A PDF or a photo of any lab report.</p></div></li>
  <li><span class="sq"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 3c0 5 10 5 10 9s-10 4-10 9M17 3c0 5-10 5-10 9s10 4 10 9M9 7h6M9 17h6"/></svg></span><div><h3>DNA</h3><p>Your 23andMe or AncestryDNA file.</p></div></li>
  <li><span class="sq"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="9" cy="10" r="5"/><circle cx="17.500" cy="7.500" r="2.500"/><circle cx="16" cy="16.500" r="3.500"/></svg></span><div><h3>Gut</h3><p>Upload a gut test report, such as Viome.</p></div></li>
  <li><span class="sq"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="4" y="4" width="16" height="16" rx="3"/><path d="M9 8.500h6M12 8.500v3"/></svg></span><div><h3>Body</h3><p>A smart scale, an InBody sheet, or values you type.</p></div></li>
  <li><span class="sq"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="6" y="7" width="12" height="10" rx="3"/><path d="M9 7l.500-4h5l.500 4M9 17l.500 4h5l.500-4"/></svg></span><div><h3>Wearable</h3><p>A screenshot of your health app that you confirm.</p></div></li>
  <li><span class="sq"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M8.500 14.500c1 1.200 2.200 1.800 3.500 1.800s2.500-.600 3.500-1.800M9 9.800v.400M15 9.800v.400"/></svg></span><div><h3>Check-ins</h3><p>How you feel each day, in about 30 seconds.</p></div></li>
  <li><span class="sq"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="6" y="4" width="12" height="17" rx="2"/><path d="M9.500 9h5M9.500 13h5M9.500 17h3"/></svg></span><div><h3>Surveys</h3><p>Eight standard questionnaires.</p></div></li>
  <li><span class="sq"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4"/><path d="M12 3v2M12 19v2M3 12h2M19 12h2M5.600 5.600l1.400 1.400M17 17l1.400 1.400M5.600 18.400L7 17M17 7l1.400-1.400"/></svg></span><div><h3>Air &amp; UV</h3><p>PM2.5, ozone, UV and weather for your city; pollen in Europe.</p></div></li>
 </ul>
 <p class="note"><b>Planned, not live.</b> Phone sync (Apple Health, Health Connect) is being prepared, Android first. Direct Oura, Whoop and Garmin links are planned.</p>
 <details><summary>What each source adds</summary><div><table>
  <tr><th>Source</th><th>What it adds</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Genetics</td><td>Variants that reshape every other signal: folate cycle, lipids, caffeine, methylation.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Wearable</td><td>HRV, sleep stages, recovery, resting heart rate, activity load.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Air &amp; UV</td><td>PM2.5, ozone, UV and weather by your location (Open-Meteo, OpenAQ, WAQI); pollen in Europe.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Check-ins</td><td>Sleep, energy, stress, diet and workload, captured as lifestyle check-ins.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Gut</td><td>Gut composition: inflammation, nutrient absorption, diet response.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Labs</td><td>CRP, ApoB, HbA1c and lipid panels: the objective check on the wearable signal.</td></tr>
 </table></div></details>
 <details><summary>Connect, normalize, encrypt: the three steps</summary><div>
  <p><b>Connect or upload.</b> Wearable data today comes from a screenshot of your health or band app that you confirm, smart-scale values, or values you type. DNA, gut and lab files are uploaded; air and UV are pulled from your location.</p>
  <p><b>Normalize into one schema.</b> Different formats (VCF, FHIR, CSV, JSON) are mapped into one queryable health schema.</p>
  <p><b>Encrypt under your key.</b> Today the profile is encrypted at rest under a per-user key that our server holds, so it can run the agent. Client-held keys (iOS Keychain, Android Keystore) are roadmap.</p>
 </div></details>
 <p><a class="tb" href="/agent">How the Lab Agent uses it</a></p>
</div></section>

<section id="evidence"><div class="wrap">
 <h2>Every recommendation cites a real source, searched live</h2>
 <p class="lead">The Lab Agent searches the literature on every run, so a plan can change when a new paper appears. Invented citations are stripped automatically.</p>
 <div class="stats">
  <div class="stat"><b>~40M</b><span>PubMed citations searched live</span></div>
  <div class="stat"><b>4</b><span>live evidence sources</span></div>
  <div class="stat"><b>5</b><span>more on the roadmap</span></div>
  <div class="stat"><b>3</b><span>labels on every link</span></div>
 </div>
 <ul class="labels">
  <li><span class="ev c">Cited</span><p>Backed by papers you can open.</p></li>
  <li><span class="ev h">Hypothesis</span><p>Likely, but the evidence is thin.</p></li>
  <li><span class="ev a">Ask your clinician</span><p>A question for your doctor.</p></li>
 </ul>
 <h3 class="sub">How a recommendation earns its citation</h3>
 <ul class="rows">
  <li><span class="sq">1</span><div><h3>Strongest</h3><p>Systematic reviews and meta-analyses, then grade A/B clinical guidelines.</p></div></li>
  <li><span class="sq">2</span><div><h3>Supporting</h3><p>Cohort studies, GWAS associations, mechanism papers.</p></div></li>
  <li><span class="sq">3</span><div><h3>Flagged</h3><p>Single studies and preprints: shown, but labelled preliminary.</p></div></li>
 </ul>
 <h3 class="sub">Where we search</h3>
 <div class="chips" aria-label="Live sources"><span class="chip sm on-lab">Live: PubMed</span><span class="chip sm on-lab">Europe PMC</span><span class="chip sm on-lab">ClinVar / dbSNP</span><span class="chip sm on-lab">GWAS Catalog</span></div>
 <div class="chips" aria-label="Roadmap sources"><span class="chip sm off">Roadmap: OpenAlex</span><span class="chip sm off">USPSTF</span><span class="chip sm off">NICE</span><span class="chip sm off">WHO</span><span class="chip sm off">Cochrane</span></div>
 <div class="tile ex"><p class="mono">Example: why "shift cardio to low-AQI hours"</p>
  <p>The MTHFR C677T variant raises sensitivity to PM2.5-driven inflammation, so timing exertion away from pollution peaks matters more.</p>
  <p><span class="ev c">Cited</span> <span class="small">PubMed PMC6068673 · meta-analysis</span></p></div>
 <p class="note"><b>No strong evidence?</b> The claim is shown and labelled, not asserted.</p>
 <details><summary>How the research search works</summary><div>
  <p><b>Searches carry names, not your data.</b> Each run searches PubMed and Europe PMC with gene, marker and condition names only. An AI judge then checks which papers support each claim.</p>
  <p><b>Matching on our server.</b> Whether a finding applies to you is matched against your profile on our server, which can read the data it processes. The Lab Agent's seven steps send the model coded facts only.</p>
  <p><b>The citation travels with the advice.</b> Each surfaced recommendation carries the source it rests on, graded by evidence strength.</p>
 </div></details>
 <details><summary>What we actually query</summary><div><p>Live today, we search PubMed (~40M citations), Europe PMC, ClinVar/dbSNP and the GWAS Catalog. On the roadmap: OpenAlex, USPSTF, NICE, WHO and Cochrane. "Cross-referenced" means we search these indexes for evidence relevant to your profile, not that millions of studies stand behind any one recommendation.</p></div></details>
 <details><summary>Three tiers, and a boundary</summary><div><p>Every insight is classified before it is shown. Evidence-backed insights carry real PMIDs, a confirmed-N-of-M corroboration check across the retrieved papers, and a High / Moderate / Emerging confidence indicator. Exploratory insights, the cross-domain connections the literature has not settled, are labelled preliminary rather than asserted. And anything clinical is withheld server-side and replaced with a warm handoff to the right clinician. For established pharmacogenomic markers (starting with CYP2C9) the published CPIC consortium guidance is shown as a descriptive reference, the one place the grade comes from a clinical consortium rather than a model.</p></div></details>
 <p><a class="tb" href="/agent#loop">The seven Lab Agent steps</a></p>
</div></section>

<section id="personalized"><div class="wrap">
 <h2>The same biology reads differently depending on your genes and where you live</h2>
 <p class="lead">The same air, the same HRV dip, the same lab value gives a different instruction for a different person.</p>
 <h3 class="sub">How a protocol is built</h3>
 <ol class="grid g3 flow3">
  <li class="tile"><span class="sq"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6h16M4 12h16M4 18h16"/></svg></span><h3>Inputs</h3><p class="small">Genotype, air and season, HRV, sleep, labs.</p></li>
  <li class="tile"><span class="sq"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6L6 18"/></svg></span><h3>Interaction</h3><p class="small">Gene and environment links are checked against the literature. Related, never caused.</p></li>
  <li class="tile"><span class="sq"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12l4 4 10-10"/></svg></span><h3>Action</h3><p class="small">A few time-bound steps, each with its evidence.</p></li>
 </ol>
 <div class="grid g2">
  <div class="tile"><p class="mono">MTHFR C677T × PM2.5</p><p class="small">Blunted homocysteine clearance plus inflammatory load from PM2.5.</p><p><span class="ev c">Cited</span> <span class="small">PubMed PMC6068673 · meta-analysis</span></p></div>
  <div class="tile"><p class="mono">APOE ε4 × PM2.5</p><p class="small">A greater neuroinflammatory response to fine particles.</p><p><span class="ev c">Cited</span> <span class="small">PubMed PMC10296707 · 2023</span></p></div>
 </div>
 <p class="cap">The evidence behind David's example below.</p>
</div></section>

<section id="case"><div class="wrap">
 <h2>25, Los Angeles, breathing on the 97th percentile</h2>
 <p class="note"><b>A fictional composite case, values illustrative.</b> The gene and environment method and the citations are real. David is an engineer in Echo Park.</p>
 <div class="stats">
  <div class="stat"><b>25</b><span>Age</span></div>
  <div class="stat"><b>p97</b><span>PM2.5 zone</span></div>
  <div class="stat"><b>TT</b><span>MTHFR C677T</span></div>
  <div class="stat"><b>3/4</b><span>APOE</span></div>
 </div>
 <p class="lead">Healthy on paper, until you connect the signals. Five sources feed his profile.</p>
 <details><summary>The VitaCrypt insight</summary><div><p>"Your MTHFR TT plus PM2.5 p97 plus a 22% HRV decline may point to low-grade inflammatory pressure on a vascular system your APOE 3/4 already taxes. Run a home HEPA purifier on high-forecast days, eat folate- and omega-3-rich foods, shift cardio to the 6 to 9am low-AQI window, and ask your clinician whether a homocysteine test and a methylated folate form make sense for you."</p></div></details>
 <details><summary>The full story</summary><div><p>David sleeps seven hours, exercises four times a week, eats well. He also lives where ambient PM2.5 routinely exceeds the WHO guideline by 5×, carries an MTHFR C677T (TT) variant that blunts folate-to-5MTHF conversion (his homocysteine runs high on a "normal" diet), and an APOE ε3/ε4 that makes him cardiovascularly sensitive to the air his commute pipes into his lungs. In the apps we reviewed we did not find one that sees both. VitaCrypt does.</p></div></details>
 <details><summary>The protocol</summary><div>
  <p><b>Diet.</b> Leafy greens and legumes for folate, oily fish for DHA, prebiotic fiber for stress-driven dysbiosis. Question for the clinician: is methylated folate (5-MTHF) right for MTHFR TT?</p>
  <p><b>Environment.</b> Suggests running a HEPA purifier when forecast AQI is above 100 and moving outdoor cardio to 6 to 9am.</p>
  <p><b>Recovery.</b> Replace one HIIT session a week with zone-2 cardio until HRV recovers by at least 10%.</p>
  <p><b>Tracking.</b> Ask your clinician about re-checking inflammatory markers in 8 weeks; new results land in the same profile.</p>
 </div></details>
 <details><summary>What leaves, and what does not</summary><div><p>In the Lab Agent, the model gets coded facts such as a marker band, a trend and a gene code, never David's name or exact values, and each send is logged. When a lab is uploaded, the report text goes to Anthropic's Claude with lines we recognise as personal removed; see <a href="/data">Your data</a>. His profile is stored encrypted under his own key, and deleting his data destroys that key.</p></div></details>
</div></section>

<section id="week"><div class="wrap">
 <h2>One person, three combinations, three protocols</h2>
 <p class="lead">David, fictional, across three moments of one week. The answer changes when the inputs change.</p>
 <ul class="grid g3">
  <li class="tile wk"><p class="mono">Tue · 06:42</p><h3>Air × MTHFR × HRV</h3><p class="small">Your air, your folate cycle and your HRV are one story.</p>
   <p class="pay"><span>DNA · MTHFR C677T</span><span>Air · PM2.5 p97</span><span>Wear · HRV ↓22%</span></p></li>
  <li class="tile wk"><p class="mono">Thu · 19:15</p><h3>Caffeine × CYP1A2 × sleep debt</h3><p class="small">Your espresso may clear slower than average.</p>
   <p class="pay"><span>DNA · CYP1A2 slow variant</span><span>Log · espresso 16:40</span><span>Sleep · debt +2.1h</span></p></li>
  <li class="tile wk"><p class="mono">Sun · 09:30</p><h3>Training × APOE × ApoB</h3><p class="small">Your training week, read next to APOE and ApoB.</p>
   <p class="pay"><span>DNA · APOE 3/4</span><span>Lab · ApoB 88 mg/dL</span><span>Load · 4× HIIT a week</span></p></li>
 </ul>
 <p class="cap">Other apps give the same advice all week. VitaCrypt re-reads the profile as signals arrive.</p>
 <details><summary>What David sees on each of the three days</summary><div>
  <p><b>Tue, air.</b> Tomorrow 14:00: PM2.5 forecast 78 μg/m³. Suggestion: run your HEPA purifier, move outdoor cardio to the 7am low-AQI window. Tonight: folate-rich dinner. Ask your clinician: is methylated folate right for MTHFR TT? Shown: PM2.5 52 μg, HRV 3-day 38 ms, CRP 3.2 mg/L, 4 PubMed citations (+5 more).</p>
  <p><b>Thu, caffeine.</b> Try no caffeine after 11:30am. You logged an espresso at 16:40 on a short-sleep week. Tonight: magnesium-rich dinner, wind-down 22:30, skip HIIT, zone-2 only. Shown: espresso 16:40, sleep debt +2.1 h, resting heart rate 64 bpm, 3 PubMed citations.</p>
  <p><b>Sun, training.</b> Next 7 days: try swapping 2× HIIT for zone-2 plus strength work, since recovery has lagged after HIIT days. Diet: olive oil, nuts, oily fish. Ask your clinician what ApoB target fits APOE 3/4. Shown: ApoB 88 mg/dL, VO2 47 ml/kg, HRV 7-day ↑4%, 6 PubMed citations (+8 more).</p>
  <p>Next steps: ask your clinician about a CRP and homocysteine retest (Tue); compare tonight's sleep in the morning check-in (Thu); ask your clinician when to retest ApoB (Sun).</p>
  <p>We have not seen these combinations in the products we reviewed.</p>
 </div></details>
 <p><a class="tb" href="/investor.html">Beta gates and dates</a></p>
</div></section>

<section id="encrypted"><div class="wrap">
 <h2>Private by design, on what is true today</h2>
 <p class="lead">Encrypted at rest under per-user keys; the Lab Agent sends a coded minimum and logs every send. Model calls go to Anthropic's Claude today. Our server can unwrap your key to run the agent; we do not claim otherwise.</p>
 <div class="grid g2 tr">
  <div class="tile"><h3>Today</h3><ul class="rows">
   <li><span class="sq"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="8" cy="15" r="4"/><path d="M11 12l9-9M17 6l3 3"/></svg></span><div><h3>Per-user keys</h3><p>Encrypted at rest; delete destroys the key.</p></div></li>
   <li><span class="sq"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12h12M12 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span><div><h3>A coded minimum</h3><p>Seven Lab Agent steps send coded facts; every send is logged.</p></div></li>
   <li><span class="sq"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12l4 4 10-10"/></svg></span><div><h3>Providers disclosed</h3><p>Listed on Your data.</p></div></li>
  </ul><p class="small">Our server holds the key so it can run the agent.</p></div>
  <div class="tile"><h3>Roadmap, not yet live</h3><ul class="rows">
   <li><span class="sq off"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12h16M4 7h16M4 17h10"/></svg></span><div><h3>Tighter minimization</h3><p>Before any external inference.</p></div></li>
   <li><span class="sq off"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="8" cy="15" r="4"/><path d="M11 12l9-9M17 6l3 3"/></svg></span><div><h3>Client-held keys</h3><p>iOS Keychain and Android Keystore.</p></div></li>
   <li><span class="sq off"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3l8 3v6c0 5-3.500 8-8 9-4.500-1-8-4-8-9V6l8-3z"/></svg></span><div><h3>Zero data retention</h3><p>From the model provider: requested, not confirmed.</p></div></li>
  </ul></div>
 </div>
 <p class="note"><b>Still true.</b> Older insight cards send a fuller profile. Zero data retention is requested, not confirmed. Early-stage MVP, pre-revenue, no outside users yet; beta users stay outside the EU and the UAE.</p>
 <details><summary>The honest status</summary><div><p>Today: encrypted at rest under per-user keys, a coded minimum to the model in the Lab Agent, and a log of every Lab Agent send. When you upload a lab, the report text goes to Anthropic's Claude with lines we recognise as personal removed; values, sex, age, test date and lab name stay, and the removal can miss an unlabelled name. Older insight cards still send the model a fuller profile; that is listed on Your data and is being fixed. Zero data retention terms are requested from the model provider, not confirmed. An OpenRouter fallback exists for model calls. The server can unwrap your key to run the agent, so it can read the data it processes. We state this plainly.</p></div></details>
 <p><a class="tb" href="/data">What happens to your data</a></p>
</div></section>

